        <h2 id="privacy">Privacy</h2>
        <p>Netria SARLAU, named above, is responsible for the personal data this site handles. The site sets no cookies and has no forms. Its pages, fonts, images and scripts are served from netria.dev itself; only the visit counter below loads anything from another company's servers.</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Server logs.</strong> GitHub records technical details of each request, including your IP address, to run and secure the service. We rely on our legitimate interest in a working, secure site. See the <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub privacy statement</a>.</li>
            <li><strong>Visit statistics.</strong> To learn which pages people read and which sites send them here, pages can load Cloudflare Web Analytics from Cloudflare, Inc. (US), which processes the data on our behalf. It receives your IP address, the page address, the page that linked to it, your browser and device type, and page-load timings. It sets no cookies and stores nothing in your browser, and we only see totals. Our dashboard shows full detail for the last 7 days, then a sample of about 10%, going back six months. See the <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare privacy policy</a>.
                <ul>
                    <li>If your device's time zone is in the EU or EEA, or isn't known, we ask first and count only if you agree: the legal basis is your consent. Time zones are only a rough guide to where you are.</li>
                    <li>Elsewhere we count by default, relying on our legitimate interest in knowing how the site is used. You can object: we don't count browsers that send Global Privacy Control, and you can turn counting off below.</li>
                    <li>Your answer is kept in your browser's local storage, so you aren't asked on every page.</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="count-setting" data-count-setting hidden></p>
            </li>
            <li><strong>Email.</strong> If you write to {{ site.email }}, we use your address and message to reply and, if we work together, to run the project: steps you asked for before a contract, and the contract itself. We keep messages while we're in touch and business records as long as Moroccan law requires. Our email is hosted by Proton AG in Switzerland; see the <a href="https://proton.me/legal/privacy">Proton privacy policy</a>.</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>Transfers.</strong> GitHub and Cloudflare process data in the United States. Both are certified under the EU–U.S. Data Privacy Framework and also rely on the European Commission's standard contractual clauses. Switzerland, where Proton is based, has an EU adequacy decision.</p>
        <p><strong>Your rights.</strong> Under Moroccan law 09-08 on personal data, and the GDPR if you are in the EU or EEA, you can ask what personal data we hold about you, have it corrected or deleted, restrict how we use it, get a copy to take elsewhere, object to processing based on our legitimate interest, and withdraw consent at any time without affecting what happened before. Write to <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>. You can also complain to a data protection authority: the CNDP in Morocco, or the authority where you live or work in the EU.</p>

        <p>Last updated 20 October 2026.</p>
